          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A clear collaborative problem and resolution, with Tansy's answering tap providing a concrete ending; some explanatory repetition makes it feel engineered rather than lively.\"},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The still-water call-and-response solution is easy to follow and ends tangibly, though the repeated technical observations slow the child-story pace.\"},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Ripples create a meaningful obstacle, and tying the pads before changing to tapping gives the resolution a strong causal progression and vivid shared-drum image.\"},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The log's low thrum and Tansy's reply make the concert solution concrete, but several setup steps repeat ideas and weaken momentum.\"},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The characters observe Tansy's needs and build a workable setup, ending with her tap, but the pads bridge is not meaningfully used in the final call-and-response performance.\"},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The rippling-water shift to tapping is sensible, but the raised sail is not integrated into the outcome and the final reference to pads and log contradicts the sail setup.\"},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A coherent still-water adaptation with a clear listener-focused ending, though it relies on repetitive explanatory dialogue rather than dramatic action.\"},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The group changes Pip's performance to fit Tansy's vibration listening, and her foot tap closes the story clearly; the prose remains somewhat formulaic and repetitive.\"},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"The pond's ripples directly cause Pip to abandon loud croaking for tapping, while the anchored log and answering foot create a satisfying, concrete finale.\"},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The rippling-water solution and visual sail are understandable, but the closing image suddenly says pads and log tremble together, contradicting the established arrangement.\"}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":3,\"ending\":1,\"language\":2,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories share the same central problem—Pip must make a concert reach vibration-listening Tansy—and the same successful endpoint of Tansy's answering tap. The modest branch is environmental: still-water stories such as s000029 and s000068 use a call-and-response song, while rippling-water stories such as s000047 and s000005 use tapping; carrier and location substitutions are otherwise mostly cosmetic. This sample does not establish diversity for the entire generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"story_ids\":[\"s000029\",\"s000057\",\"s000073\",\"s000034\",\"s000068\",\"s000096\"],\"summary\":\"In still water, the friends arrange a stable listening setup near Tansy, and Pip changes his concert into a call-and-response song that she answers by tapping.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000047\",\"s000005\"],\"summary\":\"Because pond ripples disrupt ordinary sound, the friends create an anchored vibration carrier and Pip switches from croaking to a tap rhythm that Tansy answers.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000043\",\"s000085\"],\"summary\":\"Because ripples muddle sound, Milo adds a visible leaf sail and Pip changes to tapping; Tansy answers, though the stated final arrangement inconsistently invokes pads and a log.\"}]}",
